	},
	hint = [=[Seek the stranger who waits among the Dark Iron dead, south of Thorium Point.]=],
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Velarok Windblade has come to {link:searing-gorge}the Searing Gorge{/link} for vengeance, or so he says. He tells of a father slain by the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} of {link:the-cauldron}the Cauldron{/link}, and of pleas for justice that the magistrates of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} would not hear. The kingdom, he says bitterly, would rather pretend this corner of the world did not exist than send its soldiers here. So he has come himself, with no company but a clumsy squire, and he waits for someone bold enough to help him strike.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Velarok offers what the gorge rarely does: a plan. He does not mean to fight the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} blade to blade. He means to blind them first, by burning the sentry towers that guard {link:the-cauldron}the Cauldron{/link}, and then to strike before they can recover. For those who help him, he promises riches beyond their dreams.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He tells his tale to any traveller who will listen.
• He gathers hearts of flame and golem oil for a torch that no element can quench.
• He breaks down the thorium daggers of the Dark Iron slavers to forge the torch's shaft.
• He draws the magic out of a symbol of {red:ragnaros}Ragnaros{/red}, taken from the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link}, to form its casing.]=],
		},
	},
	chapters = {
