			hint = "Gather what Velarok needs for his torch, and watch it made.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 3453 },
			},
			text = [=[The torch was made of the gorge itself. Its flame came from the hearts of fire elementals and the oil of war golems. Its shaft was forged from the enchanted thorium of the slavers' own blades. Its casing was worked from an idol of the Firelord, whose foul magic Velarok judged perfect for the task. He bent over the pieces for a long while, and bid his helper be patient. When it was done, whoever lifted the torch felt waves of hatred and anger pass through them.]=],
		},
		{
			key = "the-deceiver",
			title = "The Deceiver",
			hint = "Set the four towers of the Cauldron ablaze.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 3463 },
			},
			text = [=[The towers burned, and Velarok's squire cried out that it was glorious. Then Velarok cast off the shape of a man. He was a drake of the black dragonflight, and there had never been a murdered father. He had only needed the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}' first line of defense destroyed, and he knew that no mortal would have helped the legion of {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock{/link} if asked plainly. He spared those who had served him, so that they might live to see the chaos of the coming invasion of the gorge. He left them a hoard of trinkets, and with it the molt of a black dragon, which he said his kin in the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link} could use to fortify their craft. Then he took wing toward {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}.]=],
